              "id": "sca/untagged-leak-candidate",
              "name": "Possible side-channel leak (untagged)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Possible side-channel leak (untagged)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Table lookups indexed by key material and branches on secret values have data-dependent timing and power consumption. Tag them with `@sca(id, \"…\")` so ChipWhisperer analysis scripts can reference them with `@sca-ref(id)`, or make the code constant-time."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://chipwhisperer.readthedocs.io/",
              "help": {
                "text": "NewAE ChipWhisperer documentation <https://chipwhisperer.readthedocs.io/>\nBearSSL — Constant-time crypto <https://www.bearssl.org/constanttime.html>"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": []
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "julia/abstract-field",
              "name": "Struct field with abstract or missing type",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Struct field with abstract or missing type"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Fields typed with an abstract type (or not typed at all, i.e. `::Any`) force boxed storage and dynamic dispatch on every access, which defeats type inference and makes code using the struct more prone to invalidation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.julialang.org/en/v1/manual/performance-tips/#Avoid-fields-with-abstract-type",
              "help": {
                "text": "Performance Tips — Avoid fields with abstract type <https://docs.julialang.org/en/v1/manual/performance-tips/#Avoid-fields-with-abstract-type>\nJulia manual — Performance Tips <https://docs.julialang.org/en/v1/manual/performance-tips/>"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": []
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "julia/nonconst-global",
              "name": "Non-constant global used inside functions",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Non-constant global used inside functions"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Functions that read an untyped, non-`const` global cannot infer its type; every use becomes a dynamic lookup. Declare it `const`, give it a type (`x::Int = 0`, Julia ≥ 1.8), or wrap mutable state in a `const Ref`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.julialang.org/en/v1/manual/performance-tips/#Avoid-untyped-global-variables",
              "help": {
                "text": "Performance Tips — Avoid untyped global variables <https://docs.julialang.org/en/v1/manual/performance-tips/#Avoid-untyped-global-variables>"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": []
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "julia/untyped-container",
              "name": "Container with element type Any",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Container with element type Any"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "`[]`, `Any[]` and `Dict()` create containers with abstract element types; operations on their elements are dynamically dispatched."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.julialang.org/en/v1/manual/performance-tips/#man-performance-abstract-container",
              "help": {
                "text": "Performance Tips — Avoid containers with abstract type parameters <https://docs.julialang.org/en/v1/manual/performance-tips/#man-performance-abstract-container>"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": []
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "julia/global-in-function",
              "name": "`global` assignment inside a function",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "`global` assignment inside a function"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Writing a global from a function makes the global type-unstable and the function harder to infer."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.julialang.org/en/v1/manual/performance-tips/#Avoid-untyped-global-variables",
              "help": {
                "text": "Performance Tips — Avoid untyped global variables <https://docs.julialang.org/en/v1/manual/performance-tips/#Avoid-untyped-global-variables>"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": []
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "julia/base-method-extension",
              "name": "Extending Base/Core methods",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Extending Base/Core methods"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Adding methods to Base/Core functions for types you do not own is type piracy. Methods with abstract or untyped arguments on widely-used Base functions intersect many compiled signatures and are the most common cause of invalidations."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.julialang.org/en/v1/manual/style-guide/#Avoid-type-piracy",
              "help": {
                "text": "Julia manual — Style Guide: Avoid type piracy <https://docs.julialang.org/en/v1/manual/style-guide/#Avoid-type-piracy>\nSnoopCompile.jl — Tutorial on @snoop_invalidations <https://timholy.github.io/SnoopCompile.jl/stable/tutorials/invalidations/>"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": []
              }
            }
          ]
        }
